<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuanian Birzai Milk makes GDR issue-agencies.</title>
<headline>Lithuanian Birzai Milk makes GDR issue-agencies.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Lithuanian dairy company Birzai Milk has become the first Baltic corporate issuer of global depository receipts (GDRs) and demand outstripped supply, local news agencies BNS and ELTA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The agencies said Birzhu's issue worth $6.0 million attracted interest from 30 foreign financial institutions. Company officials were not available to confirm the reports.</p>
<p>Banks have already issued GDRs in the Baltics. Lithuania's Vilnius Bank earlier this year launched nearly $17 million of GDRs, which are quoted in Luxembourg.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
